{"code":"n4","participant":"n4 sharon","condition":"grid","name":"sharon task 2","id":"043c12cc-72f9-4d92-a4a1-900d32cebd3a","moments":{"32610eb6-4867-4c81-8358-e8dbdf4384ee":{"videoName":"A001C002_240718OR","startS":14,"endS":25,"notes":"Hi, I'm Viviana matsuda. Um, I do pottery for a living. My brand name is Mud Witch. Um, yeah. I'm a full time potter."},"992a2284-f049-475a-b3d9-d4b504db5c82":{"videoName":"A001C002_240718OR","startS":48,"endS":54.2,"notes":"dream to be a full time artist"},"7aae1a11-6003-4bc7-bf93-8167a0aa1190":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":26.2,"endS":28.5,"notes":"So my book is called Playful Pottery."},"cfbe30b2-b87a-4c22-a317-2bdc1680b6bc":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":30,"endS":37.6,"notes":"I wanted something that was a more simplified book about pottery for beginners."},"3b185f66-7705-4e11-9fa7-ed5be6b9b075":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":37.6,"endS":57.4,"notes":"I feel like what I always saw or referenced were these, like, big, hearty old school books that never really talked about color had super fun things to do in them. Um, very like old school pottery."},"21e5ef63-a1e2-4d71-b5fe-62ac8189c31f":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":86.9,"endS":98,"notes":"I hope the book provides to its readers at, um, like a good reference for just general, um, clay knowledge."},"03ed312d-16c8-47c2-953d-7f542e44d05e":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":98,"endS":107.6,"notes":"But also, I really want people to be creative and be kind to themselves."},"0c4074c3-e17d-4d9b-bec7-be4a1df26132":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":107.6,"endS":119.7,"notes":"I think that was like the main theme was creativity involves, um, being kind to yourself, which I don't think is Talked about as much as it should be."},"83102339-bbca-433e-9681-baef23e67cc4":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":119.8,"endS":130.5,"notes":"I think that there's a pressure to produce things. As a creative person, but not to be kind of kind to yourself about what the process is going to be like,"},"a6c88395-e2ae-4370-9b5a-30b3a9499697":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":133.5,"endS":147.2,"notes":"When you're kind to yourself, you are rolling with the punches. You are more open to be flexible with your designs, and you can end up with something that turns out way better than your original design."},"635e235c-d7d8-46a8-b919-974ae2097e64":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":147.4,"endS":151.6,"notes":"I think being open minded when it comes to design is really important."},"ba3887f6-593e-4dad-b5d5-d03b132beb01":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":668.9,"endS":682.5,"notes":"Um, so my voice and style for mud, which it's kind of a funny thing where when I was learning to do ceramics, I was also learning about the body positivity movement."},"2f63a428-b8ec-4655-8835-cee8d4b1bf9b":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":693.9,"endS":702.1,"notes":"And I was like starting to make these like chubby shapes and they're literally called this is the Chubby Mug. This is the Venus mug"},"96258446-6a77-4852-a017-bffa85aaae7c":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":702.3,"endS":707.8,"notes":"I think those two things kind of just mushed together the learning clay and the body positivity."},"595f7b85-7f68-48f4-846c-3af9258b4460":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":709.9,"endS":721,"notes":"they were originally supposed to be kind of like an abstract like vision of, of people, like different bodies sitting, dancing, whatever."},"8a200735-5733-425a-a45e-7f0f95337c54":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":747.2,"endS":753.7,"notes":"the style has grown into something that now is just like, fun."},"0c3b88c4-1869-4176-b366-59b32d1bcd48":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":892.3,"endS":897.1,"notes":"I think physical mediums are so important because, um, it's a way of connecting."},"65441cc0-27e4-4681-9c8f-043eb45addda":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":897.6,"endS":906.3,"notes":"Like, there's something called the artist's hand where when you, um, hand-built something or we'll throw it, you can kind of feel where the artist's hands have been."},"70671a4c-b3fc-4645-8004-6f5852640938":{"videoName":"A001C004_240718BC","startS":907.1,"endS":923.6,"notes":"and I think that that is very important because we, you know, in society, we're like, so becoming more and more disconnected to, like human interaction in especially, like, touch or anything along those lines."},"8403001e-14ca-427d-a038-584e2c06ff78":{"videoName":"B003C005_240719NB","startS":0.8,"endS":13.5,"notes":"grabbing things from shelves"},"2c88b00b-7cb4-4736-9fc3-79622f0f7265":{"videoName":"B003C006_240719KM","startS":136.4,"endS":145.1,"notes":"viviana painting"},"11031797-fff8-43a2-ad04-0387a08dfbbb":{"videoName":"B003C010_240719TX","startS":0,"endS":5.1,"notes":"mud witch sign on shelf"},"29a41782-54cf-410d-821d-ac508827a915":{"videoName":"B003C011_240719YX","startS":5.9,"endS":9.1,"notes":"shaping clay on the wheel"},"edda98e9-e620-4d69-9880-3b6a3b20579e":{"videoName":"B003C011_240719YX","startS":11,"endS":16.8,"notes":"focused"},"5dd962f0-20eb-449a-83ec-b560bb17683c":{"videoName":"B003C011_240719YX","startS":21.3,"endS":37.9,"notes":"pottery"},"920a03c9-134a-4223-944e-6f1475aaed40":{"videoName":"B003C011_240719YX","startS":68.3,"endS":84.3,"notes":"better view of her using tools"},"635e4538-46ad-4670-b4d0-ce574b1d5fc4":{"videoName":"B003C028_240719CX","startS":5.8,"endS":11.2,"notes":"borll"},"bf191275-9cbe-41c5-bdcc-777a56291338":{"videoName":"B003C028_240719CX","startS":15.1,"endS":20.8,"notes":"notes"},"b71c7792-1a57-4792-aaf0-e7c92046b8d6":{"videoName":"B003C061_240719AN","startS":19.1,"endS":24.8,"notes":"walking in"},"9b4414dc-9636-4770-bfe0-f5ab1e7482d9":{"videoName":"B003C050_240719XK","startS":7.5,"endS":19.5},"c64fa184-8144-4f2d-9e38-6677ab5068aa":{"videoName":"B003C050_240719XK","startS":19.5,"endS":27},"90f5b709-e030-445a-b563-96891384626d":{"videoName":"B003C0